Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: always-on desktop element block with periodic-table rotation
 Element Blocks Desktop pins a small chemical-element tile at a fixed position
 on the desktop. It has no taskbar entry and lives in the system tray; clicking
 the tray icon opens a settings window with a sidebar: a periodic table where
 each of the 118 elements can be enabled or disabled, and a rotation page that
 switches to the next enabled element on a chosen interval (from "never" up to
 "every day").
 .
 The Linux build uses native GTK3 widgets (no Electron, no WebView). On X11 the
 tile is a real _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_DESKTOP window; on Wayland it falls back to
 a borderless, focus-free, keep-below window because the protocol does not allow
 absolute positioning of desktop-type windows.
